# Cisco ISE MCP Server — Environment Configuration (ADVANCED / OPTIONAL)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# You normally do NOT need this file. Deployments live in a registry
# (deployments.json) that you manage with the CLI or the AI agent:
#
#     cisco-ise-mcp add --name "RADIUS Only" --host 10.1.1.1 --ers-username ers-admin
#     cisco-ise-mcp set-credential radius-only          # stores password in the OS keyring
#
# This file exists ONLY for two advanced situations:
#   1. Headless servers / Docker / Kubernetes where no OS keyring is available
#      and you want to inject passwords as environment variables.
#   2. Pointing the server at a non-default registry/cert location.
#
# Copy to ".env" if you need it. Keep it private:
#   - It is listed in .gitignore (never commit it).
#   - Restrict permissions:  chmod 600 .env   (macOS/Linux)
#
# Anything set here is read at startup via python-dotenv.

# ── Where the registry and certs live (optional override) ──
# Defaults: Windows %APPDATA%\cisco-ise-mcp ; macOS ~/Library/Application Support/cisco-ise-mcp ;
#           Linux $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cisco-ise-mcp (else ~/.config/cisco-ise-mcp).
# CISCO_ISE_MCP_HOME=/opt/cisco-ise-mcp

# ── Per-deployment password injection (headless / container alternative to keyring) ──
# The variable name is built from the deployment SLUG (lower-case name, spaces -> hyphens,
# then hyphens -> underscores, upper-cased). Examples for the sample deployments:
#
#   "RADIUS Only" -> slug radius-only -> RADIUS_ONLY
#   "TACACS Only" -> slug tacacs-only -> TACACS_ONLY
#   "VPN Only"    -> slug vpn-only    -> VPN_ONLY
#
# ERS / Open API password:
# CISCO_ISE__RADIUS_ONLY__ISE_PASSWORD=YourErsPassword
# Data Connect password (only if Data Connect is enabled for that deployment):
# CISCO_ISE__RADIUS_ONLY__DATACONNECT_PASSWORD=YourDataConnectPassword
#
# You may also point at a secret file (Docker/K8s secrets) instead of an inline value:
# CISCO_ISE__RADIUS_ONLY__ISE_PASSWORD_FILE=/run/secrets/radius_only_ise_password
# CISCO_ISE__RADIUS_ONLY__DATACONNECT_PASSWORD_FILE=/run/secrets/radius_only_dc_password

# Resolution order per deployment:  env var  ->  *_FILE  ->  OS keyring.
